<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Q1 current account surplus 7.0 bln guilders.</title>
<headline>Dutch Q1 current account surplus 7.0 bln guilders.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands posted a 7.0 billion guilder current account surplus in the first quarter of 1996, the Dutch central bank said.</p>
<p>The bank published the following figures for the current account of the Dutch balance of payments:</p>
<p>DUTCH CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95  Q3 95  Q2 95  Goods				  n.a.   9.97   6.48   7.06   8.92</p>
<p> Services			     1.57   0.30   1.57  -0.35   1.46</p>
<p> Income				-0.07  -0.96   1.17   2.09  -1.41</p>
<p> Current transfers		 -2.87  -2.29  -3.49  -2.42  -2.37</p>
<p> Current account balance	  n.a.   7.02   5.73   6.38   6.59</p>
<p>NOTES - All figures in billions of guilders. Negative sign denotes deficit.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
